The server modules
------------------

The modules are their own repositories and carry their own terms:

    mod-ledger, mod-dashboard       MIT (ours)
    mod-playerbots fork             GPL-2.0-or-later (upstream)
    mod-ollama-chat fork            AGPL-3.0 (upstream)
    mod-ah-bot-plus fork            per file; see that repository's NOTICE
    azerothcore-wotlk               GPL-2.0-or-later, unchanged
    mod-progression-system          unchanged

The combined server binary
--------------------------

AzerothCore links its modules statically, and GPL-2.0-or-later code combines
with AGPL-3.0 under GPLv3 section 13. The shipped worldserver as a whole is
therefore AGPL-3.0: anyone who runs it for other people must offer them its
source. Publishing the forks does that.

